% SHARED BIBLIOGRAPHY — norm-research
% Started 2026-07-27. Intended to be cited from any paper in latex/:
%     \bibliography{../refs-shared}          % or add to an existing list
%
% SCOPE OF THIS FILE
% This is the cross-paper bibliography for HUMAN EXPERT ARTICULATION GAPS:
% sources in which domain experts reliably agree on quality judgments but
% cannot state the criteria they use, or in which explicit stated criteria
% demonstrably fail to capture what experts actually do.
%
% It does NOT duplicate the three pre-existing bibs. Those remain:
%   methods/metric_implementer/references.bib   (771 entries; the main one)
%   notes/articulability-prompt-opt.bib         (122)
%   latex/paper-1__metric-codability/refs.bib   (51)
% See the "ALREADY HELD ELSEWHERE" index at the bottom of this file for the
% high-value articulation-gap entries that already live in those files, so
% nobody re-finds them.
%
% ANNOTATION SCHEMA
% Every entry carries an `annote` field beginning with a verification tag:
%   VERIFIED  - the quote string was confirmed present in text actually
%               fetched/OCR'd from the cited source or its publisher copy.
%   SNIPPET   - the exact string appeared in a search-result snippet or in a
%               named secondary source that quotes the primary. Trustworthy
%               enough to work with; re-check before it goes into a camera copy.
%   LEAD      - source is on-topic and real, but NO quote was obtained.
%               Never quote these. Fetch first.
% `keywords` carries: domain=...; gap=...; type=...
%   gap= taxonomy:
%     felt-not-stated   practitioner says the judgment is felt/intuited
%     stated-ne-used    stated criteria diverge from the operative ones
%     criteria-underdet written criteria underdetermine expert decisions
%     osmosis           standard transmitted by apprenticeship, not rule
%     defn-contested    the criterion is used decisively yet cannot be defined
%     confabulation     stated reasons are post-hoc constructions
%
% PROVENANCE: sweep conducted 2026-07-27, ten parallel domain agents.
% Raw per-domain sweeps (with dead ends and access notes) are archived at
%   notes/lit/2026-07-27__articulation-gap-sweeps/
% Curated quote bank organized for drafting:
%   notes/lit/2026-07-27__articulation-gap-quote-bank.md
% =====================================================================


